.bk-news h2.title {top: 0; left: 0; text-transform: uppercase; color: #288047; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 14px; border-top: none; padding-top: 0;} /* BLG-C216: $(green.color) measured 2.72:1 on this section's #F8F8FF ground; the darker green is 4.65:1. */
.bk-news h2.title:before {background: transparent; height: 0;}
.bk-news .pager-nav {top: 2px; right: 0; height: 16px;}
.bk-news .pager-nav a {padding: 3px 2px; color: $(white.color);} /* BLG-C306: the two slider arrows measured 20x23 CSS px live, under the 24x24 WCAG 2.5.8 (AA) target floor. Padding grows only the hit box; the icon does not move because padding on an inline box does not shift its content. */
.bk-news .pager-nav .uk-icon {position: relative; top: -4px;}
.post-entry-1 h3.post-title {display: inline; padding: 0 10px 0 5px; font-weight: 300;}
.post-entry-1 h3.post-title a {font-size: 14px}
.post-entry-1 .post-label a {padding: 0 2px 0 5px !important; top: -2px; border-radius: 0 !important}
.post-entry-1 .post-label a:after {content: ''; position: absolute; left: 100%; top: 0; border-top: 8px solid transparent; border-bottom: 8px solid transparent; border-left: 8px solid $(red.color);}
.post-entry-1 ul li {margin-right: 10px;}
/* BLG-C444: the operator found the featured hero title oversized against the
   other two featured cards (32px vs 20px measured live). Middle ground, not
   uniform: 24px keeps a little emphasis here, 20px under 960px below. */
.post-entry-2 h3.post-title, .post-entry-2 h3.post-title a {font-size: 24px;} /* BLG-C450: heading carries the clamp, so it takes the size too */
/* BLG-C459: main-listing, trending and sidebar-feed thumbs share the lower 68% text region with the recent block and modal (their own rules beside this one); digits live on other surfaces, untouched. */
.post-entry-2 .post-thumb.is-placeholder::after, .post-entry-3 .post-thumb.is-placeholder::after, .post-entry-4 .post-thumb.is-placeholder::after, .post-entry-5 .post-thumb.is-placeholder::after, .post-entry-12 .post-thumb.is-placeholder::after, .post-entry-13 .post-thumb.is-placeholder::after{height:68%;pointer-events:none}
/* BLG-C458: modal Most-viewed/Trending text sits lower too -- same 68% region. Breaking digits keep their own height:auto rule at higher specificity, so they stay cornered. */
#news-modal .nm-post .post-thumb.is-placeholder::after{height:68%;pointer-events:none}
.post-entry-2 .post-thumb {height: 650px;}
.post-entry-2 .post-panel, .post-entry-3 .post-panel, .post-entry-6 .post-panel, .post-entry-8 .post-panel, .post-entry-10 .post-panel {position: absolute; bottom: 0; left: 0; width: 100%}
.post-entry-2 .post-ct-panel, .post-entry-3 .post-ct-panel, .post-entry-6 .post-ct-panel, .post-entry-8 .post-ct-panel, .post-entry-10 .post-ct-panel {padding: 20px 20px 15px;
/* Gradient recipe (provenance kept; the generator's permalink URL was removed as third-party residue, BLG-C203): #03546d+0,03546d+48,012e3f+100&0+0,0.5+48,1+100 */
background: -moz-linear-gradient(top, rgba(3,84,109,0) 0%, rgba(3,84,109,0.5) 48%, rgba(1,46,63,1) 100%); /* FF3.6-15 */
background: -webkit-linear-gradient(top, rgba(3,84,109,0) 0%,rgba(3,84,109,0.5) 48%,rgba(1,46,63,1) 100%); /* Chrome10-25,Safari5.1-6 */
background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(3,84,109,0) 0%,rgba(3,84,109,0.5) 48%,rgba(1,46,63,1) 100%); /* W3C, IE10+, FF16+, Chrome26+, Opera12+, Safari7+ */
filter: progid:DXImageTransform.Microsoft.gradient( startColorstr='#0003546d', endColorstr='#012e3f',GradientType=0 ); /* IE6-9 */
}
.post-ft .post-date, .post-ft h3.post-title, .post-ft h3.post-title a, .post-ft .post-summary {color: $(white.color);} /* BLG-C450: heading carries the clamp, so it takes the colour too */
.post-entry-3 h3.post-title, .post-entry-10 h3.post-title, .post-entry-3 h3.post-title a, .post-entry-10 h3.post-title a {font-size: 20px;} /* BLG-C450: heading carries the clamp, so it takes the size too */
/* BLG-C190: the operator's request for the big card at the top of a feed block
   (the trending widget, the same shape as featured): the title belongs ON the
   photograph, and a long one should stop with an ellipsis instead of running on.

   The overlay itself was already here and was measured on the live blog before
   this line was written: the panel is absolutely positioned at the thumb's
   bottom edge (the rule above), it carries the frozen-palette scrim, and no
   media query anywhere in the skin overrides that position, so the title sits
   on the image at every width. What was missing is the clamp -- measured
   `line-clamp: none` on the live hero, so a long Marathi headline simply grew
   until it ran past the scrim, and the text below the picture in the operator's
   screenshot is a title that had outgrown its box.

   Three lines at the 20px the hero already uses, then an ellipsis. The clamp is
   written twice because the unprefixed property is the standard one and the
   prefixed one is what browsers actually honour today; without both, the rule
   works on some pages and not others. `display: -webkit-box` is part of how the
   clamp is implemented, so it is set here rather than left to the shorthand.

   overflow:hidden is the part that actually does the work, and it is here
   rather than relying on the clamp alone.

   NO max-height, and that is worth recording because the first version of this
   rule had one and the live page caught it. Measured on the operator's own
   trending hero with a long Marathi headline: before, the title box was 216px
   tall against 218px of text inside a 300px card, so the text ran out through
   the bottom of the photograph. With the rule as first written -- three-line
   clamp AND max-height 3.1em -- the box measured 50px, which is 3.1em and not
   three lines, so the max-height was the binding constraint and `overflow:
   hidden` cut the last line in half with no ellipsis at all. The operator asked
   for a title that ends in "...", and a hard cut is not that. The clamp alone
   measures exactly the three lines, and the browser paints the ellipsis
   itself. The card height is 300px before and after, because the thumb is a
   fixed height and the panel is out of flow -- a clamped title cannot make one
   card taller than the one beside it. */
.post-entry-2 h3.post-title, .post-entry-3 h3.post-title, .post-entry-6 h3.post-title,
.post-entry-8 h3.post-title, .post-entry-10 h3.post-title {
display: -webkit-box; -webkit-box-orient: vertical; -webkit-line-clamp: 3;
line-clamp: 3; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis}
